# The capture build for make graphics and make preview, and nothing else (#7).
#
# Layered over monkey.jungle rather than replacing it, so every shared setting comes from
# the one file that defines it:
#
#   monkeyc -f "monkey.jungle;graphics.jungle" ...
#
# monkeyc -f takes a semicolon-separated list and later files override earlier ones.
# This adds capture/, whose Now.mc answers the clock and the display mode from the moment
# in capture/Frame.mc, and excludes source/Now.mc's (:live) definitions of the same
# functions. Fail-closed both ways: without the exclusion, or with capture/ on another
# build's path, the build stops on a redefinition rather than compiling the frozen clock.
base.sourcePath = $(base.sourcePath);capture
# Added to, not replaced: an exclusion monkey.jungle sets (an edition's, say) still holds.
base.excludeAnnotations = $(base.excludeAnnotations);live
